1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,982
Popular accounts say that 2,400 years ago,

2
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:06,218
people in the Iranian
desert were making ice.

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,187
In summer. With no
electricity. No machines.

4
00:00:09,697 --> 00:00:12,593
Some of those ice houses
are still standing.

5
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:16,456
The oldest ones left are
younger, but the idea is ancient.

6
00:00:17,151 --> 00:00:20,153
And that is only one reason to visit Iran.

7
00:00:20,173 --> 00:00:21,304
I'll give you 7.

8
00:00:21,324 --> 00:00:26,053
One is a desert whose ground
satellites rank the hottest on Earth.

9
00:00:26,073 --> 00:00:30,894
And the secret behind that ancient
ice is still hidden underground.

10
00:00:31,721 --> 00:00:35,327
This is Iran. Close to 90 million people.

11
00:00:35,347 --> 00:00:37,292
The capital is Tehran.

12
00:00:38,203 --> 00:00:42,965
Reason 1: Isfahan. Its
great square, Naqsh-e Jahan,

13
00:00:42,985 --> 00:00:45,516
means pattern of the world.

14
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:50,615
It is 560 meters long,
with two mosques, a palace,

15
00:00:50,635 --> 00:00:54,138
and the entrance to a bazaar around it.

16
00:00:54,158 --> 00:00:57,319
It was built between 1598 and 1629.

17
00:00:58,481 --> 00:01:00,402
Reason 2: Persepolis.

18
00:01:00,422 --> 00:01:06,338
Darius the Great began this
ceremonial capital around 518 B. C..

19
00:01:07,158 --> 00:01:10,069
Alexander the Great captured it in 330 B.

20
00:01:10,089 --> 00:01:14,286
C., but its stairways and carved
stone reliefs still stand.

21
00:01:14,306 --> 00:01:17,932
And in the southwest, a
ziggurat from about 1250 B.

22
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:21,097
C. is among the best
preserved in the world.

23
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,577
Reason 3: Nowruz, the Persian New Year.

24
00:01:25,597 --> 00:01:30,301
It means new day, and it is
more than 3,000 years old.

25
00:01:30,919 --> 00:01:34,532
It starts on the first day
of spring and lasts 13 days.

26
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:37,307
Before it, families clean the whole house,

27
00:01:37,327 --> 00:01:39,837
and many people jump over small fires.

28
00:01:40,973 --> 00:01:43,849
Reason 4: the food. Start with tahdig,

29
00:01:43,869 --> 00:01:47,658
the crispy golden rice
from the bottom of the pot.

30
00:01:47,678 --> 00:01:49,812
The word means exactly that.

31
00:01:50,534 --> 00:01:55,088
Add saffron. Iran grows close
to 90% of the world's supply.

32
00:01:55,989 --> 00:02:00,838
And for dessert, faloodeh, in
Shiraz: frozen noodles, rose water,

33
00:02:00,858 --> 00:02:03,629
and lime. That is where the ice went.

34
00:02:04,277 --> 00:02:09,124
Reason 5: Yazd. The whole old
city is built of mud brick,

35
00:02:09,144 --> 00:02:13,754
and people still live in it.
UNESCO listed it in 2017.

36
00:02:14,213 --> 00:02:20,909
Look up, and you will see tall
towers that catch the breeze and
pull cool air down into the house.

37
00:02:20,929 --> 00:02:25,152
The tallest, at Dowlat Abad
Garden, is almost 34 meters high.

38
00:02:25,846 --> 00:02:30,015
But Yazd gets almost no rain. So
where does its water come from?

39
00:02:30,945 --> 00:02:32,261
Reason 6: the qanat.

40
00:02:32,281 --> 00:02:35,803
It is a tunnel that starts
at the foot of a mountain,

41
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:37,827
where water hides in the soil.

42
00:02:38,221 --> 00:02:41,605
It slopes just a little,
and gravity does the rest.

43
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:46,164
The water travels kilometers, with
no pump, and no sun to dry it up.

44
00:02:46,731 --> 00:02:52,701
The Gonabad qanat has 427 shafts
and over 33 kilometers of tunnel.

45
00:02:52,721 --> 00:02:56,060
It was dug more than 2,500 years ago.

46
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,621
And it still delivers water.

47
00:02:59,309 --> 00:03:04,252
That is the secret. The same water
filled ice pools, cooled houses,

48
00:03:04,272 --> 00:03:07,901
and fed gardens. UNESCO
lists 11 of these qanats.

49
00:03:08,754 --> 00:03:14,761
Reason 7: extremes. Mount Damavand,
a volcano higher than 5,600 meters,

50
00:03:14,781 --> 00:03:17,393
is the tallest volcano in Asia.

51
00:03:17,413 --> 00:03:19,705
And it is capped with snow.

52
00:03:20,345 --> 00:03:24,077
Then the Lut Desert, whose
name means bare, empty land.

53
00:03:24,097 --> 00:03:28,988
In 2005, a NASA satellite measured
159 degrees Fahrenheit on its ground.

54
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:34,308
A later NASA study of 18 years of data
ranked it the hottest surface on Earth,

55
00:03:34,328 --> 00:03:36,306
tied with a desert in Mexico.

56
00:03:36,609 --> 00:03:40,414
Canada currently advises
avoiding all travel to Iran.

57
00:03:40,434 --> 00:03:43,466
When that changes, this is where to start.

58
00:03:43,845 --> 00:03:46,626
Which country should we visit next?

59
00:03:46,646 --> 00:03:48,566
Tell me in the comments.

